{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218622,"nonce":"7OHwvNqisERzzQqIUbStlDgLT0A=","title":"own self: T parsed and did nothing","message":"TypedMethodParam had no ownership field, so the shared parameter rule\naccepted `own` and the annotation was dropped converting TypedFunction\nto TypedMethod, then overwritten with Default::default() in lowering. A\nmethod could not declare it consumes its receiver, so a hand-written\ndestructor was a borrow that frees. Fixed by adding the field and\ncarrying it through both zyn_peg runtimes and lowering. Bare `own self`\n(no type) was a separate grammar gap, fixed in 262a7d1.","files":null}]}